# dconf profile of the Vitre session (/usr/bin/vitre-session sets DCONF_PROFILE=vitre).
# Order is precedence, first wins: the user's own settings, then the machine-wide databases an administrator maintains (local, site:
# the same two the standard "user" profile reads; dconf ignores a database that does not exist), then the Vitre defaults. So an
# administrator's choice beats a Vitre default, and Vitre defaults beat the GSettings schema defaults and Ubuntu's overrides.
user-db:user
system-db:local
system-db:site
system-db:vitre
